Jehovah made a promise to King David of ancient Israel. That promise is called the Davidic covenant.
According to the covenant for a priest like Melchizedek, what additional assignment would the offspring have, and why?
God revealed through King David that He would personally make a covenant with Jesus. That agreement involved two things: first, Jesus would “sit at right hand ” and have the authority to conquer all of his enemies; and second, Jesus would be“ a priest forever in the manner of Melchizedek. ”
There are others who have been appointed to serve as kings and priests.
That will be discussed in the next article. Messianic Kingdom: God’s government ruled by Christ and the 144,000 anointed Christians
The woman: The heavenly part of Jehovah’s organization that is made up of loyal spirit creatures
The woman’s offspring: The primary, or main, part of the woman’s offspring is Jesus Christ. The secondary, or additional, part refers to the 144,000 anointed Christians.
The serpent: Satan the Devil The serpent’s offspring: Spirit persons and humans who take Satan’s side against God’s right to rule
The Edenic promise reveals that God will use the Kingdom to make his purpose for the earth and mankind come true. The following six covenants help to accomplish God’s purpose:
BETWEEN: Jehovah and Abraham
PURPOSE: It is the legal guarantee that the “offspring ” of“ the woman ” of Genesis 3: 15 will rule in the Kingdom
BETWEEN: Jehovah and the nation of Israel
PURPOSE: It protects the “offspring ” and helps people to identify the Messiah
BETWEEN: Jehovah and David
PURPOSE: It establishes that the Messianic King would be a descendant of David and that the Kingdom will last forever
BETWEEN: Jehovah and Jesus
PURPOSE: It is the legal guarantee that the main part of the woman’s “offspring, ” who is Jesus, will be king and priest forever
BETWEEN: Jehovah and anointed Christians
PURPOSE: It provides a legal basis for 144,000 Christians to be adopted as sons of God and to become the additional part of the “offspring ”
BETWEEN: Jesus and anointed Christians
PURPOSE: It legally unites anointed Christians with Christ to be kings and serve as priests in heaven
