What clue do we have about when the heavenly resurrection would happen? Paul’s words give us a clue as to when the heavenly resurrection would happen.
It would happen during Christ’s presence.
What will happen to some anointed ones during Christ’s presence? The Bible explains more about the heavenly resurrection: “We do not want you to be ignorant about those who are sleeping in death...
For if we have faith that Jesus died and rose again, so too God will bring with him those who have fallen asleep in death... We the living who survive to the presence of the Lord will in no way precede those who have fallen asleep in death; because the Lord himself will descend from heaven with a commanding call,... and those who are dead in union with Christ will rise first.
Afterward we the living who are surviving will, together with them, be caught away in clouds to meet the Lord in the air; and thus we will always be with the Lord. ” — 1 Thessalonians 4: 13 - 17.
